        "original_id": "a2b2e950-64f7-5309-bbf8-d8d4a23f276a",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Otto von Bismarck, Jaap J. Vermeulen\n- Plants: Bulbophyllum, Bismarckia, Bismarckia nobilis, Astragalus\n- Organizations: Orchidaceae\n- Roles: botanist\n\nFacts:\n- Otto von Bismarck was the first chancellor of the German Empire.\n- Jaap J. Vermeulen was born in 1955.\n- Jaap J. Vermeulen is a Dutch botanist who specializes in the Orchidaceae genus Bulbophyllum.\n- Bulbophyllum is the largest genus in the orchid family Orchidaceae.\n- Bulbophyllum has more than 2,000 species.\n- Bulbophyllum is one of the largest genera of flowering plants, exceeded only by Astragalus.\n- The genus Bismarckia is named for Otto von Bismarck.\n- The species epithet of Bismarckia nobilis comes from Latin for \"noble\".",
        "type": "TextSummary"
